// ============================================================================
// CYD-C5 SCENE ROOT — 320x240 LANDSCAPE (NM-CYD-C5, ST7789, backlit LCD)
// ============================================================================
//
// `build.rs` selects this file for `board-cyd-c5` and `ui/slint/shell.slint`
// for `board-waveshare-c6`. Both roots export the same `WatchShell` component
// surface — 168 properties + 55 callbacks — because `src/ui/slint_shell.rs`
// (~2,400 lines of Rust) compiles against whichever one is selected. Total
// freedom over layout; ZERO freedom over the API. `cargo check
// --no-default-features --features board-cyd-c5` compiling IS the parity test.
//
// THE ONE DESIGN DECISION THAT SHAPES EVERY PAGE: NO PERSISTENT CHROME
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// JP, 2026-08-24. The C6 shell rides a status band and a page-dot row on all
// five pages: three 78x64 RadioDots at y8..72 (30 % of a 240 px panel) plus a
// right-anchored battery pill. At 320 px wide those two OVERLAP — the pill
// lands at x~183 and MESH spans x182..260, so the pill sits inside MESH's hit
// target. There is no set of numbers that fixes it, because the collision is
// between "a status strip wide enough to read" and "a panel 90 px narrower".
//
// The decision removes the collision instead of solving it. Chrome is not
// persistent: it lives on the CLOCK page — the boot page, where a watch's
// status belongs — and PEEKS on the wake shimmer over any page. Everywhere
// else the page owns the full 320x240.
//
// The peek costs no new Rust. `hint-sides` / `hint-down` are already armed and
// sequenced by `ShellUi::hint_wake` at every wake-to-bright seam (bloom 150ms,
// fade 2600ms, destroy 3200ms); the chrome band and the page rail simply ride
// the same gate the edge hints do. So status is one wrist-raise away from any
// page, and resident on none.
//
// LANDSCAPE PUTS PAGE INDICATION ON A SIDE RAIL, NOT A BOTTOM BAND
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Width is the axis with slack (-22 % against height's -52 %). A 44 px right
// rail costs 13.75 % of the abundant axis; the C6's equivalent bottom band cost
// 44 px of the scarce one, i.e. 18 % of everything a page had. The rail is also
// where the eye already is after a horizontal page swipe.
//
// 🟥 THE CAROUSEL NO LONGER SLIDES, AND THAT IS THE DISPLAY LINK'S RULING
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The carousel's GEOMETRY survived the port untouched — it is expressed entirely
// in `pages.width` with `clip: true` and `x: (N - current-page) * pages.width`,
// the one genuinely dimension-independent structure in the C6 tree. Its MOTION
// did not.
//
// Measured arithmetic (c5-psram.md §3): a full 320x240 RGB565 repaint over this
// panel's SPI link is **61.4 ms at the vendor's 20 MHz**, and **37.2 ms even at
// the 33 MHz hard ceiling**. A full frame cannot fit a 30 ms budget at any legal
// clock, so dirty-rectangle updating is MANDATORY here — more binding than on
// the watch's QSPI AMOLED, not less.
//
// A 260 ms slide is a full-screen dirty region on every frame of it: ~4 frames
// at 61.4 ms, i.e. a 16 fps wipe with ZERO time left for rendering. So the
// `animate x` is gone from all five pages and a page change is now a HARD CUT —
// one full-frame paint, once, instead of four in a row.
//
// 🟢 That makes the carousel consistent with the launcher, which already worked
// this way and already wrote down why: *"a single hard-cut full-frame render —
// instant, no intermediate frames"*. The C6 reached that conclusion for the
// launcher from fps measurements; this panel reaches it for everything from the
// serial bit rate. Same answer, harder floor.
//
// ⚠️ The budget number that belongs at the UI level is **~117 of 240 rows per
// 30 ms, treated as OPTIMISTIC** — it is serial-bit-rate-only and excludes
// per-strip command overhead. Never design up to the line. Any "strip size"
// figures in the driver scratch docs are driver-side tuning bands, not layout
// units.
//
// HOUSE RULES THIS FILE OBEYS (each was litigated on hardware — see geom.slint)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   * ABSOLUTE positioning, `parent`-relative expressions where possible.
//     No layout managers except the fixed non-text dot rail.
//   * NEVER read a Text's own intrinsic size in a band that repaints often.
//   * PAGINATION, never `Flickable` (measured 6-11 fps on this sw renderer —
//     and now with the display link under it: a scroll's cost IS its dirty
//     region, and a shorter viewport dirties more of itself per pixel of travel).
//   * NO FULL-SCREEN MOTION. No slides, no wipes, no cross-fades. Anything that
//     animates must dirty ONE SMALL CONTIGUOUS BAND — the rule story.slint's
//     PLAY page was written under now applies tree-wide.
//   * Prefer state changes that dirty ONE contiguous region over many scattered
//     small ones: per-strip command overhead favours fewer larger rects while
//     RAM favours smaller, and the crossover is a MEASUREMENT, not an axiom.
//   * `visible:` gating, never `if`, for anything that toggles — each `if`
//     instantiates a generated inner component at ~3-6 KB.
//   * Font sizes only from the existing glyph budget.
//   * 44 px minimum touch targets (resistive XPT2046, finger-driven).
//
// PORT STATUS — 22 of 22 IN THIS BRANCH
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Every scene this root reaches is landscape-native EXCEPT the two held back at
// the bottom of this note. The other files imported from `../slint/` are the ones
// with NO absolute geometry, imported on purpose so there is exactly one copy:
//
//   theme.slint     the `Theme` global (palette, type scale, spacing, radii) and
//                   the PeerRow / WifiNet structs. ONE `global Theme` in the
//                   graph, so Rust's `set_scheme` is untouched.
//   controls.slint  seven token-driven recipes with no geometry of their own —
//                   PressTile, IconButton, Stepper, PillButton, Seg,
//                   SliderControl, OverlaySwallow. Re-authoring them would fork
//                   the touch-feedback contract that exists to live in one place.
//   launcher.slint  `LauncherTile` (Rust constructs it) and `AppIcon` — 17
//                   hand-drawn 46x46 vector glyphs shared with the app switcher.
//
// `ui/slint/scan.slint` is deliberately absent: it is the 802.15.4 Radio Scan
// page and this root never reached it on either board. Its structs live in
// theme.slint.
//
// switcher + shade: LANDED with their Rust halves (one commit, by design)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Both were held at 42dd687 until `slint_shell::switcher_slot()` /
// `shade_slot()` stopped being pure unvalidated arithmetic — at mismatched
// geometry they returned a WRONG INDEX rather than `None` (a kill-swipe kills
// the wrong session, silently). The landing commit moved the card geometry to
// `board::ui` (per-board consts, sourced from these files' port headers) and
// bounded both slot lookups by the LIVE model at the call sites, so drift now
// fails as a visible no-op. The standing rule survives: card geometry changes
// land in the scene file AND `src/board/*.rs`'s `ui` mod in the SAME commit.
// ============================================================================

import { Theme, PeerRow, WifiNet } from "../slint/theme.slint";
import { SwitcherOverlay } from "switcher.slint";
import { ShadeOverlay, NotifCard } from "shade.slint";
import { Geom } from "geom.slint";
import { RadioChip, StatusChip } from "controls_cyd.slint";

// --- landscape-native pages -------------------------------------------------
import { ClockPage } from "clock.slint";
import { PowerMenu } from "power_menu.slint";
import { VolumeOverlay } from "volume.slint";
import { LauncherOverlay, LauncherTile } from "launcher.slint";
import { SensorsPage } from "sensors.slint";
import { SystemPage } from "system.slint";
import { MeshPage } from "mesh.slint";
import { WledRemote } from "wled.slint";
import { HuntPage } from "hunt.slint";
import { ThemeOverlay } from "theme_overlay.slint";
import { EnergyPage } from "energy.slint";
import { ClimateOverlay, ClimateCard } from "climate.slint";
import { LightsOverlay } from "lights.slint";
import { PingOverlay, PingPulse } from "ping.slint";
import { PowerPage } from "power.slint";
import { VoicePage } from "voice.slint";
import { SoundLevel, SpecBand } from "soundlevel.slint";
import { SettingsHub } from "settings.slint";
import { StoryPage, StoryChapter, StorySlot } from "story.slint";

// --- PENDING: still the C6 portrait layouts (render cropped) ----------------

// Re-export so the generated Rust module keeps exposing these types —
// slint_shell.rs constructs PeerRow / LauncherTile / ClimateCard / SpecBand /
// NotifCard / WifiNet directly, and drives the scheme selector through
// `ui.global::<Theme>().set_scheme(n)`. The export list is part of the API
// contract with the C6 root: same names, same order.
export { PeerRow, ClimateCard, LauncherTile, Theme, WifiNet, SpecBand, NotifCard }

export component WatchShell inherits Window {
    width: 320px;
    height: 240px;
    background: Theme.bg;

    // --- clock ---
    in property <string> time-text: "--:--";
    in property <string> seconds-text: "--";
    in property <string> date-text: "SYNCING RTC";
    in property <float> minute-progress: 0.0;
    in property <int> steps: 0;
    in property <string> weather-text: "";
    in property <string> cpu-text: "160 MHz";
    in property <bool> gyro-on: false;
    in property <length> par-x: 0px;
    in property <length> par-y: 0px;
    // Mesh Familiar (clock nook); fed by ShellUi::set_fam.
    in property <bool> fam-known: false;
    in property <bool> fam-holding: false;
    in property <int> fam-mood: 0;
    in property <int> fam-hunger: 0;
    in property <int> fam-stage: 0;

    // sensors page (live at 100ms while showing)
    in property <string> accel-text: "--";
    in property <string> gyro-text: "--";
    in property <string> imu-temp-text: "--";
    in property <string> die-temp-text: "--";

    // system page (live at 2s while showing); chip/display are constants and
    // keep their SystemPage component defaults. fw-text is set once from Cargo.
    in property <string> fw-text: "--";
    in property <string> sigil-text: "--";
    in property <string> build-text: "--";
    in property <string> heap-text: "--";
    in property <string> uptime-text: "--";
    in property <string> battery-text: "--";

    // power page (live at 1s while showing). ⚠️ On this board the mA estimator
    // and the battery gauge have no hardware behind them (no AXP2101): the
    // properties stay in the API because slint_shell.rs writes them, but the
    // CYD power page does not display the current figures. See the port notes.
    in property <string> cpu-cell: "--";
    in property <string> display-cell: "--";
    in property <string> wifi-cell: "--";
    in property <string> ble-cell: "--";
    in property <string> imu-cell: "--";
    in property <string> audio-cell: "--";
    in property <int> total-ma: -1;
    in property <string> runtime-text: "--";
    in property <int> left-hours: 999;
    in property <string> lp-core-text: "--";

    // --- battery / radios (chrome) ---
    // `battery-percent` / `charging` stay declared (slint_shell.rs sets them and
    // removing a property breaks the build) but are NOT rendered on this board:
    // it is mains-powered, and a pill that always reads "--" is worse than no
    // pill, because a status indicator is trusted.
    in property <int> battery-percent: -1;
    in property <bool> charging: false;
    in property <bool> wifi-on: false;
    in property <bool> ble-on: false;
    in property <int> mesh-peers: 0;

    // mesh page data
    in property <string> mesh-self-text: "";
    in property <[PeerRow]> mesh-rows: [];

    // --- paging / modes ---
    in-out property <int> current-page: 0; // 0 clock 1 sensors 2 system 3 power 4 mesh
    in-out property <bool> launcher-open: false;
    in property <[LauncherTile]> launcher-tiles: [];
    in property <[string]> launcher-titles: [];
    in property <int> launcher-page-count: 1;
    in-out property <int> launcher-page: 0;
    in-out property <bool> wled-open: false;
    in property <string> wled-status: "";
    in-out property <bool> hunt-open: false;
    in property <string> hunt-seek: "SEEK --";
    in property <string> hunt-hero: "LOST";
    in property <string> hunt-arrow: "";
    in property <float> hunt-bar: 0.0;
    in property <string> hunt-rssi: "";
    in property <string> hunt-bucket: "";
    in property <bool> hunt-hot: false;
    in property <bool> hunt-found: false;
    in property <bool> hunt-warmer: false;
    in property <bool> hunt-colder: false;
    in-out property <bool> energy-open: false;
    in property <int> energy-batt: 0;
    in property <int> energy-solar-w: 0;
    in property <int> energy-grid-w: 0;
    in property <bool> energy-charging: false;
    in property <int> energy-conn: 0;
    in-out property <bool> climate-open: false;
    in property <[ClimateCard]> climate-cards;
    in property <int> climate-conn: 0;
    in-out property <int> climate-selected: -1;
    in-out property <bool> lights-open: false;
    in property <string> lights-area: "";
    in property <int> lights-on-count: 0;
    in property <int> lights-total: 0;
    in property <int> lights-status: 0;
    in property <int> lights-pending: 0;
    in-out property <bool> ping-open: false;
    in property <string> ping-peer: "";
    in property <int> ping-state: 0;
    in property <string> ping-result: "";
    in property <bool> ping-cooling: false;
    in property <bool> ping-pulse-open: false;
    in property <string> ping-pulse-from: "";
    in property <bool> ping-pulse-lit: false;
    in-out property <bool> voice-open: false;
    in property <int> voice-state: 0;
    in property <float> voice-level: 0.0;
    in property <string> voice-transcript;
    in property <string> voice-error;

    in-out property <bool> story-open: false;
    in-out property <int> story-page: 0;
    in property <[StoryChapter]> story-chapters;
    in property <bool> story-loading: false;
    in property <string> story-error;
    in property <int> story-more: 0;
    in property <string> story-play-title;
    in property <string> story-speaker;
    in property <int> story-speaker-kind: 0;
    in property <float> story-progress: 0.0;
    in property <string> story-elapsed: "0:00";
    in property <string> story-total: "0:00";
    in property <int> story-seg-index: 0;
    in property <int> story-seg-count: 0;
    in property <bool> story-playing: false;
    in property <bool> story-no-manifest: false;
    in property <bool> story-highlight-off: false;
    in property <string> story-subject;
    in property <string> story-level: "—";
    in property <string> story-xp: "—";
    in property <string> story-gold: "—";
    in property <string> story-location: "—";
    in property <string> story-status;
    in property <string> story-hp-text: "—";
    in property <float> story-hp-frac: 0.0;
    in property <bool> story-hp-known: false;
    in property <[StorySlot]> story-equipment;
    in property <[StorySlot]> story-appearance;
    in property <bool> story-paused: false;
    in property <int> story-equipped-count: 0;
    in property <int> story-appearance-count: 0;
    in-out property <bool> mic-open: false;
    in property <float> mic-dbfs: -60;
    in property <float> mic-peak: -60;
    in property <[SpecBand]> mic-spectrum: [];
    in property <int> mic-gain-db: 0;
    in-out property <bool> theme-open: false;
    in-out property <bool> settings-open: false;
    in-out property <int> settings-page: 0;
    in property <int> net-view: 0;
    in property <bool> touch-sound-on: true;
    in property <bool> mesh-enabled: false;
    in property <bool> wifi-intent: false;
    in property <int> node-id: 0;
    in property <string> ota-status: "";
    in property <string> net-current: "";
    in property <int> net-status: 0;
    in property <bool> net-scanning: false;
    in property <[WifiNet]> wifi-nets: [];
    in property <string> kb-title: "";
    in property <string> kb-context: "";
    in property <string> kb-text: "";
    in property <bool> kb-plain: false;
    in property <string> boot-short-action: "Volume +";
    in property <string> boot-long-action: "Launcher";
    in property <string> pwron-short-action: "Volume \u{2212}";
    in property <string> pwron-long-action: "Power menu";
    in property <bool> volume-overlay-open: false;
    in property <int> volume-level: 11;
    in property <bool> volume-muted: false;
    in-out property <float> volume-frac: 0.73;
    in-out property <bool> switcher-open: false;
    in property <[LauncherTile]> switcher-tiles: [];
    in property <int> switcher-count: 0;
    in property <int> suspended-count: 0;
    in-out property <bool> shade-open: false;
    in property <[NotifCard]> notif-cards: [];
    in property <int> notif-total: 0;
    in property <int> notif-unread: 0;
    in property <bool> hint-sides: false;
    in property <bool> hint-up: false;
    in property <bool> hint-down: false;
    in property <bool> hints-lit: false;
    in property <bool> aod: false;
    in property <string> toast-text: "";
    in-out property <bool> power-menu-open: false;
    in property <bool> vbus-on: false;

    // --- callbacks (drained by the Rust loop via request cells) ---
    callback brightness-changed(float);
    callback wifi-tap();
    callback ble-tap();
    callback mesh-tap();
    callback cpu-tap();
    callback gyro-tap();
    callback reboot-tap();
    callback launch-app(int);
    callback wled-emit(int);
    callback wled-close();
    callback hunt-next();
    callback hunt-close();
    callback energy-close();
    callback climate-set-temp(int, float);
    callback climate-set-mode(int, int);
    callback climate-closed();
    callback lights-cmd(int);
    callback lights-closed();
    callback ping-send();
    callback ping-pulse-tap();
    callback voice-ptt-pressed();
    callback voice-ptt-released();

    callback story-nav(int);
    callback story-pick(int);
    callback story-stop();
    callback story-pause();
    callback story-resume();
    callback story-note();
    callback story-page-prev();
    callback story-page-next();
    callback mic-gain-down();
    callback mic-gain-up();
    callback theme-changed(int);
    callback touch-sound-tap();
    callback settings-ota-tap();
    callback net-open();
    callback net-pick(int);
    callback net-manual();
    callback net-back();
    callback kb-key(string);
    callback kb-bksp-down();
    callback kb-bksp-up();
    callback kb-eye();
    callback kb-done();
    callback button-cycle(int);
    callback volume-down();
    callback volume-up();
    callback volume-mute-tap();
    callback volume-changed(float);
    callback power-shutdown-tap();
    callback open-switcher();
    callback switcher-resume(int);
    callback open-shade();
    callback notif-dismiss(int);
    callback notif-clear();

    in-out property <float> brightness: 0.8;
    // Rust-pushed backlight on-state (CydBacklightToggle isel workaround).
    in property <bool> backlight-on: true;
    // Board identity (Luna's §1d): Rust formats these from board::*/capability
    // features at scene create; no shared scene hardcodes a board fact again.
    in property <string> board-chip;
    in property <string> board-mem;
    in property <string> board-caps;
    in property <bool> backlight-dimmable;
    in property <bool> has-boot-key;

    // ==================== takeover gate (#75) ====================
    // Carried over verbatim from the C6 root, and it matters MORE here, not
    // less. The software renderer has no occlusion culling: it builds a scene
    // item per glyph and per rectangle behind an opaque cover, so hidden
    // content costs exactly as much per-frame heap as visible content.
    //
    // ⚠️ Scene-item counts do NOT shrink with the panel. Pixels drop 63 %
    // (205,820 -> 76,800) but items are per-element, and `PrepareScene`'s Vecs
    // grow by DOUBLING — so the 256/128/128 rungs that OOM at 54-66 kB free
    // (#75) sit exactly where they did. Every one of those measurements has to
    // be RE-TAKEN on this board, never scaled from the C6 numbers.
    property <bool> covered-invisibly: root.launcher-open || root.settings-open
        || root.wled-open || root.hunt-open || root.energy-open
        || root.climate-open || root.lights-open || root.ping-open
        || root.voice-open || root.mic-open || root.theme-open
        || root.power-menu-open || root.aod;

    property <bool> covered: root.covered-invisibly
        || root.shade-open || root.switcher-open
        || root.story-open;

    // ---- RULE, learned the hard way (0685985) ----------------------------------
    // NEVER gate an element on `covered` if that element can only become visible
    // BECAUSE a covered surface is up. Three toasts fire only while an overlay is
    // up ("No WiFi credentials — set in Settings" is raised by a WIFI tap, which
    // by construction happens with `settings-open == true`), so gating the toast
    // made that button silently dead. Before adding `!root.covered` to anything,
    // grep for who SETS it, not just where it sits in z.
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

    // The wake peek. `hint-sides` / `hint-down` are armed and sequenced by
    // ShellUi::hint_wake on the render clock; this shell only draws. Reusing
    // that gate for the chrome band is what makes "no persistent chrome"
    // cost zero new Rust.
    property <bool> peek: root.hint-sides || root.hint-down;
    // Chrome is on the clock page always, and everywhere else only in the peek.
    property <bool> chrome-shown: !root.covered
        && (root.current-page == 0 || root.peek);
    // On the clock page it is solid; on a peek it rides the hint tween.
    property <float> chrome-alpha: root.current-page == 0
        ? 1.0 : (root.hints-lit ? 1.0 : 0.0);

    // Page backdrop. On the dark schemes `Theme.bg` is solid #000000. NOTE for
    // this panel: black is no longer free. The C6 comment called true black
    // "self-emissive, battery-optimal" — that is an AMOLED property. The ST7789
    // is BACKLIT, so a black page costs exactly what a white one does. It is
    // kept because it looks right and the palette is shared, not to save power.
    Rectangle {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        background: Theme.bg;
    }

    pages := Rectangle {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        clip: true;
        // #75: one `visible` on the container culls all five pages' draw AND
        // input in a single check.
        visible: !root.covered;

        ClockPage {
            x: (0 - root.current-page) * pages.width;
            width: pages.width; height: pages.height;
            time-text: root.time-text;
            seconds-text: root.seconds-text;
            date-text: root.date-text;
            minute-progress: root.minute-progress;
            steps: root.steps;
            weather-text: root.weather-text;
            cpu-text: root.cpu-text;
            gyro-on: root.gyro-on;
            par-x: root.par-x;
            par-y: root.par-y;
            fam-known: root.fam-known;
            fam-holding: root.fam-holding;
            fam-mood: root.fam-mood;
            fam-hunger: root.fam-hunger;
            fam-stage: root.fam-stage;
            cpu-tap => { root.cpu-tap(); }
            gyro-tap => { root.gyro-tap(); }
            apps-tap => { root.launcher-open = true; }
        }

        SensorsPage {
            x: (1 - root.current-page) * pages.width;
            width: pages.width; height: pages.height;
            board-chip: root.board-chip;
            board-mem: root.board-mem;
            board-caps: root.board-caps;
            accel-text: root.accel-text;
            gyro-text: root.gyro-text;
            imu-temp-text: root.imu-temp-text;
            die-temp-text: root.die-temp-text;
            steps: root.steps;
        }

        SystemPage {
            x: (2 - root.current-page) * pages.width;
            width: pages.width; height: pages.height;
            board-chip: root.board-chip;
            fw-text: root.fw-text;
            sigil-text: root.sigil-text;
            build-text: root.build-text;
            heap-text: root.heap-text;
            uptime-text: root.uptime-text;
            battery-text: root.battery-text;
        }

        PowerPage {
            x: (3 - root.current-page) * pages.width;
            width: pages.width; height: pages.height;
            cpu-cell: root.cpu-cell;
            display-cell: root.display-cell;
            wifi-cell: root.wifi-cell;
            ble-cell: root.ble-cell;
            imu-cell: root.imu-cell;
            audio-cell: root.audio-cell;
            total-ma: root.total-ma;
            runtime-text: root.runtime-text;
            left-hours: root.left-hours;
            lp-core-text: root.lp-core-text;
            brightness <=> root.brightness;
            backlight-on: root.backlight-on;
            backlight-dimmable: root.backlight-dimmable;
            brightness-changed(f) => { root.brightness-changed(f); }
            reboot-tap => { root.reboot-tap(); }
        }

        MeshPage {
            x: (4 - root.current-page) * pages.width;
            width: pages.width; height: pages.height;
            self-text: root.mesh-self-text;
            rows: root.mesh-rows;
        }
    }

    // ==================== gesture hints (wake shimmer) ====================
    // Four TIGHT edge strips — deliberately NOT one full-screen container — so
    // the opacity tween's dirty region stays small under the partial renderer.
    // Re-anchored for landscape: the side strips shrink 100 -> 72 px tall
    // (30 % of this axis, same fraction of the panel the C6 pair had) and the
    // top/bottom handles move to the real edges of a 240 px panel.
    //
    // ⚠️ The BOTTOM handle is the visual half of a Rust constant. Its Rust half
    // is `EDGE_BOTTOM_Y = 427` in slint_shell.rs — entirely off a 240 px panel,
    // which makes bottom-edge swipe-up (launcher) and hold-to-switcher
    // UNREACHABLE until it moves. Proposed value: 204. See
    // `ui/cyd/PROPOSED-board-ui-consts.patch`.

    // Left edge: page carousel, more content behind the left bezel.
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.hint-sides && !root.covered;
        x: 0; y: 84px; width: 30px; height: 72px;
        opacity: root.hints-lit ? 1.0 : 0.0;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }
        Rectangle { // aurora bar hugging the bezel
            x: 2px; y: 8px; width: 3px; height: 56px; border-radius: 1.5px;
            background: Theme.accent2.with-alpha(0.45);
        }
        Text { // primary chevron
            x: 8px; y: 0; height: parent.height; vertical-alignment: center;
            text: "\u{2039}"; color: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.85);
            font-size: 30px;
        }
        Text { // trailing echo — the page sliding in
            x: 18px; y: 0; height: parent.height; vertical-alignment: center;
            text: "\u{2039}"; color: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.3);
            font-size: 30px;
        }
    }

    // Right edge: mirror of the left strip. Sits UNDER the page rail's x-range
    // by design — they are never both up in a way that reads as clutter (the
    // rail is 6 px of tick, the strip is a chevron pair at the bezel).
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.hint-sides && !root.covered;
        x: parent.width - self.width; y: 84px; width: 30px; height: 72px;
        opacity: root.hints-lit ? 1.0 : 0.0;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }
        Rectangle {
            x: parent.width - 5px; y: 8px; width: 3px; height: 56px;
            border-radius: 1.5px;
            background: Theme.accent2.with-alpha(0.45);
        }
        Text {
            x: parent.width - self.width - 8px;
            y: 0; height: parent.height; vertical-alignment: center;
            text: "\u{203a}"; color: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.85);
            font-size: 30px;
        }
        Text {
            x: parent.width - self.width - 18px;
            y: 0; height: parent.height; vertical-alignment: center;
            text: "\u{203a}"; color: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.3);
            font-size: 30px;
        }
    }

    // Bottom edge: edge-swipe up -> launcher (#29).
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.hint-up && !root.covered;
        x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2; y: 214px;
        width: 104px; height: 22px;
        opacity: root.hints-lit ? 1.0 : 0.0;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }
        Rectangle { // echo — narrower and fainter, "rising"
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2; y: 3px;
            width: 48px; height: 4px; border-radius: 2px;
            background: Theme.accent2.with-alpha(0.5);
        }
        Rectangle { // the handle
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2; y: 12px;
            width: 84px; height: 5px; border-radius: 2.5px;
            background: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.9);
        }
    }

    // Top edge: edge-swipe down -> notification shade (#32).
    //
    // ⚠️ This is the one hint the landscape re-composition genuinely squeezed,
    // and it is worth stating why rather than leaving the numbers to be read as
    // arbitrary. On the C6 the handle sat at y2..28 ABOVE the radio dots, whose
    // visible row starts ~y38 — 36 px of clear bezel to draw in. Here the
    // chrome band's visible content starts at y6 and its chips span x8..318, so
    // there is no clear span left: not centred (lands on BLE), not right (lands
    // on the status chips), not below (that is content).
    //
    // So the handle collapses to a 4 px hairline in the top 6 px — the only
    // pixels the chrome band does not claim. It reads as an edge, which is what
    // it means, and it drops the "descending echo" because a 6 px band cannot
    // express motion. It stays INSIDE the proposed `EDGE_TOP_Y = 44` zone, so
    // the affordance is where the gesture actually is.
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.hint-down && !root.covered;
        x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2; y: 0;
        width: 104px; height: 6px;
        opacity: root.hints-lit ? 1.0 : 0.0;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }
        Rectangle { // the handle
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2; y: 1px;
            width: 84px; height: 4px; border-radius: 2px;
            background: Theme.accent.with-alpha(0.9);
        }
    }

    // ==================== chrome band (NOT persistent) ====================
    // One container, so the whole band is a single `visible` check, a single
    // opacity tween, and a single dirty region rather than five.
    //
    // Row arithmetic, stated because it is the number the C6 chrome could not
    // make work: three 70 px radio chips at x 8 / 80 / 152 end at x 222, and
    // two 44 px status chips at x 228 / 274 end at x 318. Total 320 with 6 px
    // of slack — where the C6 needed 330 in 320 and overlapped. What bought
    // the room: labels lose the battery pill (no PMU on this board, and a pill
    // reading "--" forever is worse than none) and `MESH·4` replaces `MESH 4`.
    //
    // The band is 44 px of hit area (the touch floor) presenting a 28 px visual
    // at y 6..34 — the chips pad their own TouchAreas outward rather than
    // growing the visual. Transparent container, so it consumes nothing: a
    // plain Rectangle does not eat clicks, which is the same fact
    // `OverlaySwallow` exists to work around.
    //
    // ⚠️ THIS IS THE LARGEST ANIMATED REGION LEFT IN THE TREE, and it is
    // deliberately the only full-WIDTH one. 320x44 is **44 of the ~117
    // full-width rows** a 30 ms paint can afford — 38 % of an optimistic budget,
    // for ~8 frames of a 480 ms tween.
    //
    // It survives the no-full-screen-motion rule on three grounds, all of which
    // have to hold together:
    //   * 44 rows is a BAND, not a screen. The rule is one small contiguous
    //     region, and this is one contiguous region.
    //   * It only ever tweens on a PEEK over a non-clock page. On the clock page
    //     `chrome-alpha` is the constant 1.0, so no tween is triggered at all —
    //     the resident case costs nothing.
    //   * A peek is armed by `hint_wake`, which fires at a wake-to-bright seam:
    //     nothing else is repainting and there is no audio in flight.
    // If any of those three stops being true, this becomes a hard cut (delete
    // the `animate` line) and the peek simply appears.
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.chrome-shown;
        x: 0; y: 0;
        width: parent.width;
        height: Geom.chrome-hit;
        opacity: root.chrome-alpha;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }

        RadioChip {
            x: Geom.safe-side; y: Geom.chrome-y;
            label: "WIFI"; active: root.wifi-on;
            tapped => { root.wifi-tap(); }
        }
        RadioChip {
            x: 80px; y: Geom.chrome-y;
            label: "BLE"; active: root.ble-on;
            tapped => { root.ble-tap(); }
        }
        RadioChip {
            x: 152px; y: Geom.chrome-y;
            label: root.mesh-peers > 0 ? "MESH\u{00b7}\{root.mesh-peers}" : "MESH";
            active: root.mesh-peers > 0;
            tapped => { root.mesh-tap(); }
        }

        // Unread notifications (#32) and suspended apps (#31). `visible:`-gated
        // rather than `if`-gated: each `if` would cost a ~3-6 KB generated
        // inner component, and these are chrome that is resident anyway.
        StatusChip {
            visible: root.notif-unread > 0;
            x: 228px; y: Geom.chrome-y;
            glyph-kind: 1;
            count: root.notif-unread;
            tapped => { root.open-shade(); }
        }
        StatusChip {
            visible: root.suspended-count > 0;
            x: 274px; y: Geom.chrome-y;
            glyph-kind: 0;
            count: root.suspended-count;
            tapped => { root.open-switcher(); }
        }
    }

    // ==================== page rail (NOT persistent) ====================
    // Five ticks on the RIGHT EDGE, vertical. Tap advances, exactly as the C6
    // bottom dot row did — but on the axis with slack. Same gate as the chrome
    // band: resident on the clock page, a peek everywhere else.
    //
    // 44x88 hit area (the floor on both axes) presenting six-pixel ticks at
    // x 305..311. It overlaps page content in x, which is safe BECAUSE it is
    // gated: `visible: false` culls hit-testing as well as draw — verified on
    // the C6 by dispatching a pointer press at a covered control and observing
    // that the callback does not fire.
    //
    // The tick column is the one layout manager in this file. That is the
    // sanctioned exception: a small, fixed-size, NON-TEXT element row, which is
    // the same thing the C6 dot row does. Layout managers size children from
    // their intrinsic dimensions, which for `Text` is the 16 B-per-read
    // allocation two recent commits exist to delete — so no text goes near one.
    rail := TouchArea {
        visible: root.chrome-shown;
        x: parent.width - 44px;
        y: (parent.height - 88px) / 2;
        width: 44px;
        height: 88px;
        opacity: root.chrome-alpha;
        animate opacity { duration: 480ms; easing: ease-in-out; }
        clicked => { root.current-page = mod(root.current-page + 1, 5); }
        VerticalLayout {
            x: 33px;
            y: (parent.height - 70px) / 2;
            spacing: 10px;
            for i in 5: Rectangle {
                width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px;
                background: root.current-page == i ? Theme.accent
                    : (rail.pressed ? Theme.soft : Theme.line);
            }
        }
    }

    // ==================== launcher overlay ====================
    if root.launcher-open: LauncherOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        tiles: root.launcher-tiles;
        titles: root.launcher-titles;
        page-count: root.launcher-page-count;
        page <=> root.launcher-page;
        launch-app(idx) => { root.launch-app(idx); }
    }

    // ==================== WLED remote overlay ====================
    if root.wled-open: WledRemote {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        status: root.wled-status;
        emit(a) => { root.wled-emit(a); }
        close => { root.wled-close(); }
    }

    // ==================== Hunt overlay ====================
    if root.hunt-open: HuntPage {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        seek-text: root.hunt-seek;
        hero-text: root.hunt-hero;
        arrow: root.hunt-arrow;
        bar-frac: root.hunt-bar;
        rssi-text: root.hunt-rssi;
        bucket: root.hunt-bucket;
        hot: root.hunt-hot;
        found: root.hunt-found;
        warmer: root.hunt-warmer;
        colder: root.hunt-colder;
        next-target => { root.hunt-next(); }
        close => { root.hunt-close(); }
    }

    // ==================== Energy overlay ====================
    if root.energy-open: EnergyPage {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        battery-pct: root.energy-batt;
        solar-w: root.energy-solar-w;
        grid-w: root.energy-grid-w;
        charging: root.energy-charging;
        conn-state: root.energy-conn;
        close => { root.energy-close(); }
    }

    // ==================== Climate overlay (#58) ====================
    if root.climate-open: ClimateOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        cards: root.climate-cards;
        conn-state: root.climate-conn;
        selected-index <=> root.climate-selected;
        set-temp(id, t) => { root.climate-set-temp(id, t); }
        set-mode(id, m) => { root.climate-set-mode(id, m); }
        closed => { root.climate-closed(); }
    }

    // ==================== Lights overlay (#39) ====================
    if root.lights-open: LightsOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        area: root.lights-area;
        on-count: root.lights-on-count;
        total-count: root.lights-total;
        status: root.lights-status;
        pending: root.lights-pending;
        cmd(a) => { root.lights-cmd(a); }
        closed => { root.lights-closed(); }
    }

    // ==================== Ping overlay (#35) ====================
    if root.ping-open: PingOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        peer: root.ping-peer;
        state: root.ping-state;
        result: root.ping-result;
        cooling: root.ping-cooling;
        mesh-on: root.mesh-enabled;
        send => { root.ping-send(); }
        closed => { root.ping-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Voice overlay ====================
    // ⚠️ NO MIC ON THIS BOARD. Kept declared (slint_shell.rs references every
    // member) but dropped from the launcher registry rather than stubbed, per
    // JP: an app that renders and cannot work is a bug report waiting to be
    // filed. The overlay is unreachable, not absent.
    if root.voice-open: VoicePage {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        voice-state: root.voice-state;
        level: root.voice-level;
        transcript: root.voice-transcript;
        error-text: root.voice-error;
        ptt-pressed => { root.voice-ptt-pressed(); }
        ptt-released => { root.voice-ptt-released(); }
        close => { root.voice-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Story overlay (#story) ====================
    if root.story-open: StoryPage {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        page: root.story-page;
        chapters: root.story-chapters;
        loading: root.story-loading;
        error-text: root.story-error;
        more-count: root.story-more;
        play-title: root.story-play-title;
        speaker: root.story-speaker;
        speaker-kind: root.story-speaker-kind;
        progress: root.story-progress;
        elapsed: root.story-elapsed;
        total: root.story-total;
        seg-index: root.story-seg-index;
        seg-count: root.story-seg-count;
        playing: root.story-playing;
        no-manifest: root.story-no-manifest;
        highlight-off: root.story-highlight-off;
        subject: root.story-subject;
        level: root.story-level;
        xp: root.story-xp;
        gold: root.story-gold;
        location: root.story-location;
        status: root.story-status;
        hp-text: root.story-hp-text;
        hp-frac: root.story-hp-frac;
        hp-known: root.story-hp-known;
        equipment: root.story-equipment;
        appearance: root.story-appearance;
        paused: root.story-paused;
        pause => { root.story-pause(); }
        resume => { root.story-resume(); }
        equipped-count: root.story-equipped-count;
        appearance-count: root.story-appearance-count;
        nav(p) => { root.story-nav(p); }
        pick(n) => { root.story-pick(n); }
        stop => { root.story-stop(); }
        note => { root.story-note(); }
        page-prev => { root.story-page-prev(); }
        page-next => { root.story-page-next(); }
        close => { root.story-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== SoundLevel meter overlay ====================
    // ⚠️ NO MIC. Same treatment as Voice: declared, dropped from the launcher.
    if root.mic-open: SoundLevel {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        mic-dbfs: root.mic-dbfs;
        mic-peak: root.mic-peak;
        spectrum: root.mic-spectrum;
        gain-db: root.mic-gain-db;
        gain-down => { root.mic-gain-down(); }
        gain-up => { root.mic-gain-up(); }
        close => { root.mic-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Theme picker overlay ====================
    if root.theme-open: ThemeOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        changed(n) => { root.theme-changed(n); }
        close => { root.theme-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Settings hub (v0.9.0) ====================
    if root.settings-open: SettingsHub {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        page <=> root.settings-page;
        net-view: root.net-view;
        touch-sound: root.touch-sound-on;
        gain-db: root.mic-gain-db;
        brightness <=> root.brightness;
        backlight-on: root.backlight-on;
        backlight-dimmable: root.backlight-dimmable;
        has-boot-key: root.has-boot-key;
        ble-on: root.ble-on;
        mesh-on: root.mesh-enabled;
        wifi-intent: root.wifi-intent;
        wifi-live: root.wifi-on;
        net-current: root.net-current;
        net-status: root.net-status;
        scanning: root.net-scanning;
        nets: root.wifi-nets;
        kb-title: root.kb-title;
        kb-context: root.kb-context;
        kb-text: root.kb-text;
        kb-plain: root.kb-plain;
        sigil: root.sigil-text;
        fw: root.fw-text;
        build: root.build-text;
        node-id: root.node-id;
        ota-status: root.ota-status;
        volume-level: root.volume-level;
        volume-muted: root.volume-muted;
        boot-short-action: root.boot-short-action;
        boot-long-action: root.boot-long-action;
        pwron-short-action: root.pwron-short-action;
        pwron-long-action: root.pwron-long-action;
        toggle-touch-sound => { root.touch-sound-tap(); }
        gain-down => { root.mic-gain-down(); }
        gain-up => { root.mic-gain-up(); }
        vol-down => { root.volume-down(); }
        vol-up => { root.volume-up(); }
        vol-mute => { root.volume-mute-tap(); }
        button-cycle(s) => { root.button-cycle(s); }
        brightness-changed(f) => { root.brightness-changed(f); }
        ble-tap => { root.ble-tap(); }
        mesh-tap => { root.mesh-tap(); }
        wifi-tap => { root.wifi-tap(); }
        net-open => { root.net-open(); }
        net-rescan => { root.net-open(); }
        net-pick(i) => { root.net-pick(i); }
        net-manual => { root.net-manual(); }
        nav-back => { root.net-back(); }
        close => { root.settings-open = false; }
        ota-tap => { root.settings-ota-tap(); }
        kb-key(k) => { root.kb-key(k); }
        kb-bksp-down => { root.kb-bksp-down(); }
        kb-bksp-up => { root.kb-bksp-up(); }
        kb-eye => { root.kb-eye(); }
        kb-done => { root.kb-done(); }
    }

    // ==================== Power menu (#48) ====================
    // ⚠️ NO PMU. `power-shutdown-tap` has no hardware path to power off on this
    // board; deep sleep is the plausible substitute and is a firmware decision,
    // not a layout one. The menu still owns REBOOT, which works.
    if root.power-menu-open: PowerMenu {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        battery-percent: root.battery-percent;
        charging: root.charging;
        vbus-on: root.vbus-on;
        reboot-tap => { root.reboot-tap(); }
        shutdown-tap => { root.power-shutdown-tap(); }
        close => { root.power-menu-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== App switcher (#31) ====================
    if root.switcher-open: SwitcherOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        tiles: root.switcher-tiles;
        count: root.switcher-count;
        resume(i) => {
            root.switcher-open = false;
            root.switcher-resume(i);
        }
        close => { root.switcher-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Notification shade (#32) ====================
    if root.shade-open: ShadeOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        cards: root.notif-cards;
        total: root.notif-total;
        dismiss(i) => { root.notif-dismiss(i); }
        clear-all => { root.notif-clear(); }
        close => { root.shade-open = false; }
    }

    // ==================== Ping receiver pulse (#35) ====================
    if root.ping-pulse-open: PingPulse {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        from: root.ping-pulse-from;
        lit: root.ping-pulse-lit;
        dismissed => { root.ping-pulse-tap(); }
    }

    // ==================== Volume HUD (#59) ====================
    if root.volume-overlay-open: VolumeOverlay {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        level: root.volume-level;
        muted: root.volume-muted;
        frac <=> root.volume-frac;
        changed(f) => { root.volume-changed(f); }
    }

    // ==================== AOD overlay ====================
    // Landscape AOD: the 84 px hero fits comfortably on the wide axis (a 5-glyph
    // "12:34" is ~230 px of 320) where it took 45 % of the C6's vertical budget.
    // Kept at 84 rather than dropped to 66 like the clock hero, because AOD is
    // read at arm's length and has the whole panel to itself.
    if root.aod: Rectangle {
        width: 100%; height: 100%;
        background: #000000;
        Text {
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
            y: 58px;
            text: root.time-text;
            color: #6b7690;
            font-size: 84px;
            font-weight: 300;
        }
        Text {
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
            y: 166px;
            text: root.date-text;
            color: Theme.faint;
            font-size: 18px;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
        }
    }

    // ==================== Toast — MUST BE LAST ====================
    //
    // ⚠️ POSITION IS LOAD-BEARING — do not move this block up.
    //
    // It used to sit above the overlay conditionals on the C6 root. Later
    // siblings paint on top, every full-screen overlay draws an opaque
    // `Theme.bg` backdrop first, and the software renderer has no occlusion
    // culling — so the toast's glyphs were built into the scene and then
    // completely overpainted. Proof: `story(page0)` and
    // `story(page0,+toast31)` rendered BYTE-IDENTICAL PPMs while the scene grew
    // by 32 items and 31 glyphs. Full price, zero pixels.
    //
    // Also deliberately NOT `covered`-gated, for the reason in the RULE above:
    // three of its emit sites can only fire while an overlay IS up.
    //
    // Landscape: 300 px max width (was 360 — off-panel here) and raised to
    // y 186 so a 36 px card clears the bottom edge with the safe inset.
    Rectangle {
        visible: root.toast-text != "";
        x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
        y: 186px;
        width: min(300px, toast-label.width + 32px);
        height: 36px;
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: #1a2233ee;
        border-width: 1px; border-color: Theme.line;
        toast-label := Text {
            x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
            y: 0;
            height: parent.height;
            vertical-alignment: center;
            text: root.toast-text; color: Theme.ink; font-size: Geom.t-body;
        }
    }
}
